The C++ and Python tutorials demonstrate the standalone Ariadne Integration API.

Build Ariadne Integration and install it to a prefix, then configure this directory
with that prefix in CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH. The tutorial includes ariadne-integration.hpp
and links against the installed ariadne-integration library.

Both tutorials include the common ValidatedIntegrationRequest / ValidatedIntegrationStep
contract, two consecutive steps for an equation and a structured differential inclusion,
retrieval of reach sections and endpoint maps, and explicit rejection of unsupported
field capabilities. Python wrappers keep borrowed fields and backends alive; C++
examples use named objects for those dependencies.
